                <pb facs="0483" n="398" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg398"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.015315/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jones</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-16T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your telegram December 9, 4 p.m. and despatch No. 72 of December 16.</p>
                <p>Should you not have received satisfactory reply to your note of December 11 to
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs, you will request immediate suitable amends from
                    Honduran Government for insult to flag.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
